---
description: >-
  Exercises automatic text wrapping (via wrappingWidth/minNodeWidth) versus
  manual <br/> line breaks for the same long label text across a wide variety of
  node shapes, including classic shapes (rounded rectangle, stadium, circle,
  diamond, triple-circle) and new @{ shape: ... } syntax shapes (diamond,
  display, delay, dbl-circ, curv-trap, half-rounded-rectangle).
config:
  fontFamily: courier
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 120
    minNodeWidth: 120
---
flowchart TD
  R[Choose how to continue from here] --> S([Choose how to continue from here])
  R --> C((Choose how to continue from here))
  R --> D{Choose how to continue from here}
  S --> B([First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line])
  C --> Q((First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line))
  D --> A@{ shape: diamond, label: "First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line" }
  B --> T(Choose how to continue from here)
  Q --> T
  A --> T
  R --> DC(((Choose how to continue from here)))
  R --> DP@{ shape: display, label: "Choose how to continue from here" }
  R --> DL@{ shape: delay, label: "Choose how to continue from here" }
  DC --> DCB@{ shape: dbl-circ, label: "First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line" }
  DP --> DPB@{ shape: curv-trap, label: "First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line" }
  DL --> DLB@{ shape: half-rounded-rectangle, label: "First chosen line<br/>Second chosen line" }
